{
  "title": "8W8",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "TR-808 style drum",
        "machine. 16 voices,",
        "all synthesized,",
        "no samples.",
        "",
        "Kick, snare, toms,",
        "congas and clap are",
        "circuit models. The",
        "rest are checked",
        "against sc808 to",
        "within -64 dB."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Playing",
      "lines": [
        "Pads (left 4x4):",
        " r1: BD SD LT MT",
        " r2: HT LC MC HC",
        " r3: RS CL MA CP",
        " r4: CB CH OH CY",
        "",
        "16 drums, so no",
        "Master pad - reach",
        "it with the jog.",
        "Shift+Pad: select",
        " without sounding.",
        "Mute+Pad: mute that",
        " drum ([M] in bar)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Editing",
      "lines": [
        "Knobs 1-8 edit the",
        "page on screen.",
        "Jog: next page.",
        "Shift+Jog: jump",
        " section.",
        "Jog click: section",
        " list.",
        "Shift: show values",
        " and fine mode.",
        "Mute+knob: reset",
        " that pot.",
        "Jog click on Main:",
        " locks the page.",
        " Pads still play,",
        " page stays put.",
        " ([L] in the bar)",
        " Shift+Pad still",
        " selects. Click",
        " again to unlock."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The voices",
      "lines": [
        "Every voice is the",
        "808's own circuit,",
        "from the service",
        "notes. There is no",
        "engine switch any",
        "more - each lane",
        "passed on hardware",
        "and the choice has",
        "an answer.",
        "",
        "KICK: Decay is LOOP",
        " GAIN, so the pitch",
        " sighs and fast",
        " repeats never",
        " machine-gun.",
        "SNARE: two shells,",
        " 173 and 336 Hz.",
        " Snappy sets the",
        " noise length too.",
        "TOMS: one bridged-T",
        " ringing in a loop.",
        " Decay is SECONDS.",
        "CLAP: three bursts",
        " 10 ms apart into a",
        " 330 ms tail.",
        "METAL: six free-",
        " running oscillators",
        " shared by the hats,",
        " cymbal and cowbell,",
        " so no two hits are",
        " the same.",
        "RIM: the one voice",
        " that is not the",
        " circuit - two were",
        " built and both lost",
        " by ear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Every page",
      "lines": [
        "Every drum has Tune,",
        "Decay, Drive, a",
        "Distortion type,",
        "Level, and (bar the",
        "kick) Rev and Dly.",
        "",
        "Defaults are what",
        "the hardware does -",
        "not pot centre.",
        "Mute+knob resets it.",
        "",
        "Rim and Clave have",
        "a pad each."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Choke",
      "lines": [
        "The 808 shares one",
        "metal source between",
        "the hats, so closed",
        "cuts open. Here it",
        "is a switch:",
        " Off / CH>OH /",
        " Mutual.",
        "On the Closed Hat",
        "page and on Master."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Distortion",
      "lines": [
        "Per drum and across",
        "the kit: Diode,",
        "Clip, SAT, BFZ,",
        "PDIST, Fold, Crush.",
        "The same seven as",
        "9W9 and 6W6, so the",
        "knob means the same",
        "on all three.",
        "",
        "DRIVE fully DOWN is",
        "exactly dry - the",
        "stage is not in the",
        "path at all, and",
        "that is the default.",
        "",
        "The knob adds",
        "saturation, not",
        "level.",
        "",
        "Master Dist has an",
        "Off position."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sequencing",
      "lines": [
        "Use Move's own",
        "sequencer: a drum",
        "track with a kit,",
        "muted (HiJack),",
        "track MIDI OUT on",
        "the slot's channel.",
        "",
        "Notes 36-50, one",
        "lane per drum, or",
        "General MIDI -",
        "switch on Master."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Velocity",
      "lines": [
        "Velocity sets the",
        "level all the way up",
        "- no accent switch,",
        "no step in the",
        "middle. 127 is the",
        "loudest it gets.",
        "",
        "VELOCITY on Master",
        "is how far a soft",
        "hit falls below it.",
        "0 = every hit the",
        "same. It only ever",
        "carves DOWN.",
        "",
        "On most voices it is",
        "a trigger VOLTAGE -",
        "a hard hit is a",
        "different sound and",
        "not just a louder."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reverb + Delay",
      "lines": [
        "Two send buses, one",
        "page each - reach",
        "them with the jog.",
        "",
        "Every drum has REV",
        "and DLY on its own",
        "page. The KICK does",
        "not: a dry kick is",
        "the point, and the",
        "low end is what the",
        "send HPF keeps out",
        "of the wet path.",
        "",
        "Sends are post-",
        "fader: what you",
        "hear is what you",
        "send.",
        "",
        "DELAY TIME is a",
        "note division and",
        "follows the host",
        "tempo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comp",
      "lines": [
        "One knob of bus",
        "glue on Master.",
        "Not 808 - the",
        "machine had none.",
        "",
        "It walks threshold,",
        "ratio and makeup",
        "together, so",
        "loudness stays put",
        "while the gap",
        "between loud and",
        "quiet passages",
        "closes.",
        "",
        "At 0 it is not in",
        "the path at all.",
        "That is the",
        "default."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Remote panel",
      "lines": [
        "A full 808 panel in",
        "a browser: every",
        "instrument at once,",
        "as columns.",
        "",
        "Port 7700 then",
        "/remote-ui, while",
        "8W8 is the slot's",
        "synth.",
        " move.local:7700",
        " 172.16.254.1:7700"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
